<title>LEBANON: Lebanon has $141.1 mln BoP surplus in October.</title>
<headline>Lebanon has $141.1 mln BoP surplus in October.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon had a $141.1 million balance of payments surplus in October, $104.4 million above the September surplus and the October 1995 surplus of $87.2 million, the Bank of Lebanon said in its latest monthly bulletin.</p>
<p>&quot;This surplus in the Balance of Payments is due to sustained net capital inflows,&quot; the Bank said.</p>
<p>    BALANCE OF PAYMENTS    Oct 96	Sept 96     Oct 95</p>
<p>    Monthly		     141.1	   36.7	 87.2</p>
<p>    Year to date		463.4	  322.3	 83.0</p>
<p>Annual results</p>
<p>    1995	 256</p>
<p>    1994     1,130.5</p>
<p>    1993     1,169.5</p>
<p>Note - Figures in millions of U.S. dollars, surplus unless indicated by minus sign.</p>
<p>- Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 353078 861723</p>
